; Psychonauts' menus on the DS4 (milestone k, docs/ps4/HANDOFF-i.md): keyboard mode, temporary until milestone l
; switches the profile to xinput (the game's own pad support). The menus take the arrow keys, Enter and Escape;
; the first launch's new-profile screen (the bunk bed and the name) takes only Enter and Esc. The laptop run of
; milestone j found the menus wanting Space once the pad's bindings were lost, so triangle sends Space as a
; second confirm. Gameplay is not laid out here: no movement or camera keys until l.
;
;   up down left right  the arrow keys    move through the menus
;   left stick          the arrow keys    the same, as four held keys past a 40% push
;   cross               enter             confirm (and the name screen)
;   circle              escape            back (and the name screen)
;   options             escape            back, the game's menu
;   triangle            space             confirm, as the menus took it on the laptop
;   right stick                           the mouse pointer
;   r2 / r1             mouse_left / mouse_right
;   touchpad                              the title's marks (the title keeps it unbound): a tap marks the menu
;   create (Share)                        unbound: the PS4 system takes it for its share menu
[input]
mode = keyboard
mouse = right_stick
mouse_speed = 600
keyboard_stick = left_stick
stick_deadzone = 40
stick_up = up
stick_down = down
stick_left = left
stick_right = right
up = up
down = down
left = left
right = right
cross = enter
circle = escape
options = escape
triangle = space
r2 = mouse_left
r1 = mouse_right
